From 6de462fc8a8eb45fe92ab43357e39e5ffda2d716 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FileP fork <fork@local>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:33:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] app: select the item after "open location"

Opening a search result's location navigated to its folder but never selected
the file: the reveal intent rode on the tab's pending-selection fields, which
navigation invalidates (ClearSelection + selection_revision bump), so
TakeListingSelection() treated them as stale and overwrote them with the now
empty selection before anything was restored. On top of that, the pane path is
display text (C:\dir) while selection paths are extended (\\?\C:\dir\file),
so comparing the target folder to the current one never matched.

Keep the intent in its own request (folder + names, short deadline) and apply
it once per view-model build when the tab really lists that folder. Used by the
search-result menu verb and by the staging tray's "show in folder".
